<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39715" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pū^trĭdus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		putreo. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Rotten</i>, <i>corrupt</i>, <i>decayed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimis jam putrida membra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					2, 141</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si quid in nucleo putridi fuerit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 4, 45, § 88</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cadaver,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 14, 19</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Withered</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					64, 352</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Hor. Epod. 8, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
